@cc [owner:jchen0824,label:security;api] connectors-api-enabled-provider-guard
When `CONNECTORS_ENABLED_PROVIDERS` is set, a handler that creates a connector, or that can start
work for a connector or provider (a workflow, a sync, a provider-side write), MUST refuse every
provider the list does not enable, through `checkConnectorProviderEnabled` or
`withEnabledConnectorProviders`, before any side effect: no connector row, no OAuth or credential
call, no workflow. Pausing, deleting and read-only handlers stay available for every provider. When
the variable is unset, handlers behave as upstream.

@cc [owner:jchen0824,label:security;testing] connectors-api-enabled-provider-guard-coverage
`enabled_connector_providers.test.ts` MUST list every route that `startServer` registers, in
`GUARDED_ROUTES` or in `UNGUARDED_ROUTES`. A route whose handler is guarded by
`checkConnectorProviderEnabled` or `withEnabledConnectorProviders` MUST be in `GUARDED_ROUTES`,
sent through the app `startServer` builds, with a request that its guard refuses with 403 and no
side effect when the list does not enable the route's provider, and that reaches the handler when
the variable is unset.
